   "date": "2018-05-09T07:57:22Z",
   "subject": "time stratified analysis - time slices in wrong place",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Nick, <div>using your example script as a template, I have attempted to run a time stratified analysis. All input file formats are corresponding with your templates. However, in the PDF output, the time slices as indicated by dashed lines are not in the place where they should be according to the definitions of the input file timeperiods.txt (0.1 - 0.24 - 0.47 - 0.66 - 0.83 - 1.1). Instead, they all sit much deeper in time. My question: Is this a problem relating to the drawing of the PDF graphic or does this indicate that the time slices are somehow incorrectly applied in the analyses. And how can I fix this? Thanks, Frank (Attachments: Biogeobears skript, timeperiods.txt, PDF output example)</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "2BRPnh6bAAAJ",
   "from": "Nick Matzke",
   "author": "115d05260b0c341a",
   "date": "2018-05-10T00:04:26Z",
   "subject": "Re: [BioGeoBEARS] time stratified analysis - time slices in wrong place",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi -- I can take a look, but you will need to also send the geography file, tree file, and whatever other time-stratified files you were using (changing distances or whatever).<div><br></div><div>It&#39;s possible that something about the new APE is messing with the display (and/or something about the short timescale).</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers!</div><div>Nick</div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, May 9, 2018 at 7:57 PM, Frank Koehler <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">frank....@austmus.gov.au</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Nick, <div>using your example script as a template, I have attempted to run a time stratified analysis. All input file formats are corresponding with your templates. However, in the PDF output, the time slices as indicated by dashed lines are not in the place where they should be according to the definitions of the input file timeperiods.txt (0.1 - 0.24 - 0.47 - 0.66 - 0.83 - 1.1). Instead, they all sit much deeper in time. My question: Is this a problem relating to the drawing of the PDF graphic or does this indicate that the time slices are somehow incorrectly applied in the analyses. And how can I fix this? Thanks, Frank (Attachments: Biogeobears skript, timeperiods.txt, PDF output example)</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
