     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bioge...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bioge...@googlegroups.com</a>]\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Nick Matzke<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Monday, 21 May 2018 1:11 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bioge...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Re: [BioGeoBEARS] time stratified analysis - time slices in wrong place<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\">Hi Frank -- thanks for sending the files.</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\">The issue is just this: your input tree had a root.edge, you can see it if you do:</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"background:white\">trfn = (&quot;mcmc_tree.tre&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"background:white\">tr = read.tree(trfn)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\">names(tr)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\">You can remove it if you do:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\">tr$root.edge = NULL<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\">write.tree(tr, file=&quot;mcmc_tree2.tre&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\">...and use that as the new input tree.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\">It looks like the plotting function (which has to convert ages-before-present into ages-from-the-bottom-of-the-tree) mistakenly assumes that the bottom of the tree\r\n will always be the root node, rather than the bottom of the root edge.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\">I can fix this at some point, but for now it is easier to fix your tree.  This error is just about plotting, so the base analysis should not be effected.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\">Cheers!<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\">Nick<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222;background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><div><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On Thu, May 10, 2018 at 12:04 PM, Nick Matzke &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nickmat...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><div><div><blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0cm 0cm 0cm 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-right:0cm\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi -- I can take a look, but you will need to also send the geography file, tree file, and whatever other time-stratified files you were using (changing distances or whatever).<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">It&#39;s possible that something about the new APE is messing with the display (and/or something about the short timescale).<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Cheers!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#888888\">Nick<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#888888\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><div><div><blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0cm 0cm 0cm 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-right:0cm\"><div><div><div><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On Wed, May 9, 2018 at 7:57 PM, Frank Koehler &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">frank....@austmus.gov.au</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><div><div><blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0cm 0cm 0cm 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-right:0cm\"><div><div><div><div><blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0cm 0cm 0cm 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-right:0cm\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi Nick, <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">using your example script as a template, I have attempted to run a time stratified analysis. All input file formats are corresponding with your templates. However, in the PDF output, the time slices as indicated by dashed lines are not\r\n in the place where they should be according to the definitions of the input file timeperiods.txt (0.1 - 0.24 - 0.47 - 0.66 - 0.83 - 1.1). Instead, they all sit much deeper in time. My question: Is this a problem relating to the drawing of the PDF graphic or\r\n does this indicate that the time slices are somehow incorrectly applied in the analyses. And how can I fix this? Thanks, Frank (Attachments: Biogeobears skript, timeperiods.txt, PDF output example)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
